  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_031, acc=0.678) uses scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted. All multimodal experiments so far have used resnet50 as the image encoder, leaving the image-encoder choice (resnet50 vs. imagenet_vit_l) completely unexplored. This is a high-impact design axis because ViT-L is a substantially more powerful, architecture-distinct image encoder. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l improve performance when combined with the already-optimized RNA encoder (scvi_n200), multiprofile, avgpool, and weighted fusion? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable change from the current best, isolating the image-encoder effect. A positive result would identify a new promising direction; a null or negative result would let us rule out ViT-L across all remaining configurations, saving multiple future experiments under the limited budget. The other untested axes (transformer aggregation, concat fusion) have weaker priors for improvement given the consistent avgpool>transformer and weighted>concat trends observed with PCA, making them lower-information choices."
